How these are wired into the build:
- `build.rs` maps the Rust target triple to the ABI directory and emits
  `cargo:rustc-link-search=native=vendor/android-libs/<abi>`, because `libmpv2-sys`
  emits only a bare `cargo:rustc-link-lib=mpv` (no pkg-config, no search path).
- `Cargo.toml` carries `[package.metadata.android] runtime_libs = "vendor/android-libs"`,
  which makes cargo-apk add `<runtime_libs>/<android_abi>/*.so` to `lib/<abi>/`
  of the APK (checked against cargo-apk 0.9.6 + ndk-build 0.9.0 sources). Both
  paths point at the same files, so the linked and the packaged copy cannot
  drift apart.
- Only ABIs with a vendored file here are linkable; `build.rs` warns (instead of
  leaving an obscure `cannot find -lmpv`) for any other Android target.

Notes:
- Only `lib/<abi>/libmpv.so` is vendored. Each jar also contains
  `lib/<abi>/libmediakitandroidhelper.so` (media-kit's own JNI bridge), which we
  do not use: our render path is the `mpv_render_*` GL underlay in
  `src/player.rs`, and `readelf -d` confirms `libmpv.so` has no `NEEDED` on the
  helper (only system libs: libm, libandroid, libOpenSLES, libEGL, libdl, libc;
  SONAME is `libmpv.so`). The OpenSL ES dependency is what backs `ao=opensles`
  for audio out on-device.
- Directory names are Gradle Android ABI names (`arm64-v8a`, `x86_64`), matching
  the jar layout, ndk-build's `target.android_abi()` and cargo-apk's
  `runtime_libs` convention. They intentionally differ from the Rust target
  triples (`aarch64-linux-android`, `x86_64-linux-android`).
- The `full` flavor is a superset of `default`; the extra codecs are subtitle
  bitmap decoders (PGS, XSUB, JACOsub, …) plus more audio/video decoders. It
  was chosen because `default` cannot play HDMV PGS subtitles at all.
- To upgrade: download the new tag's `full-<abi>.jar`s, verify sizes, extract
  `lib/<abi>/libmpv.so` over these files, and update this table. Keep `full`:
  switching back to `default` silently drops PGS/bitmap subtitle playback.
